Interview findings (inputs that shaped the build)

Role: Data/AI/Analytics specialist, within Software/tech
Primary AI use cases: data analysis/dashboards/reports, building AI-powered tools/prototypes, coding & debugging
Biggest bottleneck: iterating/debugging AI output that's "close but not right"
Primary model: GPT/ChatGPT
Experience level: Intermediate — comfortable with prompting, wants more structure/reuse
Desired outcome: faster iteration loops (getting to correct output quicker), not just better organization
Explicit request: include a Daily Tasks section for recurring work (standups, reviews, data pulls)

Category structure derived from the above (5, not generic defaults)

Data Analysis & Reporting
AI Prototyping & Tools
Coding & Debugging
Iteration & Refinement — created specifically because "iterating on close-but-wrong output" was the stated #1 bottleneck; holds the "diagnose the gap before regenerating" and "compare two outputs" workflows
Daily Recurring Tasks

Seed content

10 pre-built workflows, 2 per category, each with: editable {{variable}} template, example use, best practices, tags, favorite/copy actions
Iteration category workflows directly target the stated bottleneck rather than being generic filler

Core interactive systems built

Prompt Builder: 9 modular blocks (role, objective, context, constraints, reasoning strategy, output format, tone, examples, quality checks) — each with a plain-language "what it does / why it matters" description shown both in the picker and once added, live-updating preview, copy, save-as-workflow
Loop Builder: converts any base prompt into a self-evaluating loop via goal, evaluation criteria, improvement strategy (dropdown), stop conditions, and safety rules — with the term "autonomous loop" explicitly defined in-UI on first appearance
Daily Tasks: recurring task tracker with frequency + optional link to a saved workflow

"Unmistakable purpose" requirements — how each was satisfied

Persistent explainer banner on Dashboard, dismissible only via its own close button, describing the tool and every section in plain language
Always-visible "What is this?" button in both the sidebar and top bar, reopens the full explainer modal anytime
Plain nav labels throughout (Dashboard, Workflows, Prompt Builder, Loop Builder, Daily Tasks, Favorites) — no invented jargon
Empty states and subtitles written as plain descriptions of purpose (e.g. "Your saved AI prompt workflows, at a glance"), not decorative copy

SaaS-polish features included

Dark/light theme toggle, responsive layout (collapsing sidebar on mobile)
Keyboard shortcuts: / search, n new workflow, g d/w/p/l navigate, t theme, ? shortcuts help
3-step onboarding modal on first load (skippable, won't reappear)
Full CRUD (create/edit/duplicate/favorite/search/filter) on workflows, backed by localStorage
Import/export as JSON for portability across browsers/machines

Known trade-offs / things not exhaustively covered

Seed workflows are illustrative starting points, not an exhaustive library — the design intent (per the brief) is that the Prompt Builder + Loop Builder generate the "thousands of variations," not a large static prompt list
No external libraries/fonts used — typography relies on system font stacks styled via CSS custom properties, per the "no external dependencies" constraint
All data is local-only (localStorage); there's no sync across devices/browsers by design
